WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.190
What happened?

3
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:18.310
What the fuck do we do now. Manuel?
The whole Army will be on our ass!

4
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.710
- God has already shown me the way.
- And what is this fucking way?

5
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.710
MONTERREY. MEXICO

6
00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.630
Why don't you wait for me upstairs?

7
00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.590
- I'll be right up with a drink.
- Yeah.

8
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.510
How old is she?

9
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.910
You're all over the news. asshole.

10
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.430
The shipment left safe and sound.

11
00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.870
I did my job.

12
00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.630
What do you want?

13
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.070
A meeting with the Leyras.

14
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.510
You're too hot to go near them now.

15
00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.790
It's not a question.

16
00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.270
What's all this?
You think I give a shit about her?

17
00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.750
Kill her.
Kill her. motherfucker. Go on!

18
00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.910
I think you're misunderstanding
our presence here.

19
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:24.670
You're a dead man. asshole.
You and all your shitbag men. Get it?

20
00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.870
How do you think we got in?

21
00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:32.430
By politely asking your goons
if we could have a chat with you?

22
00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.470
Mexico trained us to be the best.
And we are.

23
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.550
That's why I want to suggest

24
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.750
you make life easier
for your bosses. the Leyras.

25
00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.670
or make it more difficult for them.

26
00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.150
Why don't you cut the bullshit

27
00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:59.390
and tell me what the fuck
you're doing in my house?

28
00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.910
I already told you. a meeting.

29
00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.470
Or else?

30
00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.150
Or else...

31
00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.750
I'll boil you alive.

32
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.590
Starting with your feet

33
00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.950
and when they're cooked.

34
00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.230
I'll cut them off

35
00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:24.870
and I'll keep you alive
so you can eat them.

36
00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.830
right down to the toenails.

37
00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.030
What do you say?

38
00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:43.550
- Hello. Chief. Who are these guys?
- They came to see the boss.

39
00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.590
Open up. motherfucker.

40
00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.310
Open up.

41
00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.270
God has told me that our future
lies in your organization.

42
00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:24.630
You can tell your God that a bunch
of ex-soldiers don't do me any good.

43
00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.910
We don't see things
from the same perspective. sir.

44
00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:33.190
What perspective
are you talking about. Manuel?

45
00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.870
You aren't taking advantage
of your dominance in the marketplace.

46
00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.670
You keep selling wholesale
when you could be selling retail.

47
00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:47.990
So you're suggesting
to pay the dealers on every street?

48
00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.030
That's impossible.

49
00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:54.710
You don't have to pay them.
you just have to control them.

50
00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.870
And that's our expertise.

51
00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.990
And you need all these men for this?

52
00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.670
Who is the least skilled?

53
00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:15.590
- We're all skilled.
- I didn't ask that. The least skilled...

54
00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.310
One. two. three...

55
00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:24.950
I'll pick four.

56
00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:28.990
The fifth... we'll kill him.

57
00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.950
Well. I say... we'll kill this one.

58
00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:40.510
This little shit. okay?
But I don't know. you decide.

59
00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:47.710
What?
We need men who obey.

60
00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:53.110
- You need loyal men.
- Loyal to us. asshole! Come on.

61
00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.710
- Easy!
- Shoot. asshole. shoot!

62
00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.590
I'll wipe out everyone
you've ever known!

63
00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:03.590
Jacinto...

64
00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.390
We came here to work.

65
00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.310
All of us.

66
00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:15.670
God wants it this way.

67
00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:22.790
Let's talk. Manuel.

68
00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:25.630
ZEROZEROZERO

69
00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:35.150
THE ALTLANTIC OCEAN

70
00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:38.670
There's no way we can take the ship
to Gioia Tauro.

71
00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:42.190
Our best bet is to do
what the Mexican said.

72
00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:46.430
Trans-ship in the port of Dakar.
get a clean boat and finish that way.

73
00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:51.110
Until then. we shut down AIS and
INMARSAT and we stay out of sight.

74
00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.390
Okay.

75
00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.430
Chart a course for Senegal.

76
00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:02.030
Sounders. I want full speed.
all the way there.

77
00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:05.030
- Add whatever watches you need.
- Yes. sir.

78
00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:14.430
I was boarded by pirates once.

79
00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:22.150
It was many years ago.
when your father still liked to sail.

80
00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.190
Six of them boarded.
held us at gunpoint.

81
00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:31.550
Your father was a tougher man
than anyone had ever met. but...

82
00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.590
when you have a rifle
between the eyes...

83
00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:43.030
There is no such thing
as a hero at sea.

84
00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:25.710
- Mister Lynwood. can I help you?
- I just want to see it in action.

85
00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.790
- You need ear protection.
- I know.

86
00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:11.350
I was just in the aux engine room.
And I noticed there was oil everywhere.

87
00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.910
And I went over to the cylinders.

88
00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.590
And they were loose.
they were pouring oil.

89
00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.470
I'm sure somebody just missed it
on the maintenance check.

90
00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:24.110
No. every single one of the filters
was loose.

91
00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:27.310
If we hit rough waters.
started up those engines

92
00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:29.230
there'd be a fire in ten minutes.

93
00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:32.030
I know what I am talking about.
you know that.

94
00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.030
I grew up on your boats.

95
00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.350
I tend not to assume malice
when stupidity's on the table.

96
00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.150
They didn't just loosen themselves.

97
00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:46.950
Don't worry. I've been working
with those guys for many years.

98
00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:50.230
Your father knows them.

99
00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.470
All of them.

100
00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.590
Luzvimino. right?

101
00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.830
- You work in the oil room?
- Yes. sir.

102
00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:27.990
Nice boat. isn't it?

103
00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.350
We thought about going
with a two-stroke.

104
00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:35.030
but after looking at the start-up cost
we decided to go with this one.

105
00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.270
Do you need something.
Mr. Lynwood?

106
00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:58.390
Why are you trying
to start an engine fire?

107
00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:01.550
What do you mean?

108
00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:05.670
I have you on tape unscrewing the oil
cylinders on one of the aux engines.

109
00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:09.990
- I don't know what you're talking about.
- Don't fuck with me!

110
00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:15.310
I need you to tell me
what the fuck is going on.

111
00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.630
Why are you trying
to burn down my ship?

112
00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:26.550
He told me to do it. I'm sorry. pal.
I'm sorry. sir. I'm sorry.

113
00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.390
Who told you?

114
00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:31.870
Who the fuck told you?

115
00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.990
The Chief engineer.

116
00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.830
Have you talked
to anyone about this?

117
00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.590
No. I came straight to you.
but we need to call Emma.

118
00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:52.350
No!
It's too dangerous.

119
00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:54.950
Anything with the transmitter
stays off until we unload.

120
00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:57.630
- I need to tell her what's going on.
- You don't need to tell her anything.

121
00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.430
Fuck.

122
00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.710
Fuck! Help!
Fuck!

123
00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:31.030
Fuck!

124
00:26:02.990 --> 00:26:06.390
NEW ORLEANS. U.S.A.

125
00:26:46.750 --> 00:26:48.230
You need a ride home.

126
00:27:00.630 --> 00:27:03.150
How long have you been doing
this work?

127
00:27:06.310 --> 00:27:07.710
Since I was 20.

128
00:27:11.190 --> 00:27:12.510
I love the sea.

129
00:27:12.950 --> 00:27:17.070
You can see the Strait of Messina
from my window.

130
00:27:19.310 --> 00:27:21.190
I hate the sea.

131
00:27:24.710 --> 00:27:28.310
I hate these new mega ships
that sail on their own.

132
00:27:28.510 --> 00:27:34.110
the Filipino crews paid peanuts
who don't even know what the sea is.

133
00:27:35.870 --> 00:27:42.030
It wasn't like that before.
When I started. it was all different.

134
00:27:43.310 --> 00:27:45.030
Turn right. here.

135
00:28:01.790 --> 00:28:03.350
Why don't you quit?

136
00:28:04.390 --> 00:28:06.630
- What else could I do?
- Enjoy life.

137
00:28:10.990 --> 00:28:14.270
We can get you 100.000 dollars
the day after tomorrow.

138
00:28:15.390 --> 00:28:18.750
And a million euros when it's done.
wherever you want.

139
00:28:25.550 --> 00:28:26.830
What do you want?

140
00:28:27.790 --> 00:28:31.710
We want to be sure the shipment
never gets to Gioia Tauro.

141
00:28:38.430 --> 00:28:40.630
- How?
- I don't care how.

142
00:28:42.990 --> 00:28:46.430
What matters is that no one
ever knows it was you or us.

143
00:28:49.590 --> 00:28:53.390
- Edward Lynwood was my friend.
- Now he's dead.

144
00:28:57.950 --> 00:28:59.350
Right?

145
00:29:08.270 --> 00:29:13.230
REGGIO CALABRIA. ITALY

146
00:29:20.630 --> 00:29:23.030
What's your brother's wife
doing here?

147
00:29:23.190 --> 00:29:24.510
Where's Nicola?

148
00:29:24.590 --> 00:29:27.790
- He was supposed to meet us.
- Your brother didn't come home.

149
00:29:27.990 --> 00:29:31.390
He's been missing since yesterday.
he's not answering his phone.

150
00:29:31.590 --> 00:29:34.470
He had to see a guy.
but I don't know who.

151
00:29:35.670 --> 00:29:37.070
Come with Uncle.

152
00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:40.790
It's your fuckin' grandfather.

153
00:30:46.710 --> 00:30:48.590
What a lovely parmigiana!

154
00:30:51.390 --> 00:30:52.830
The American's back.

155
00:30:53.190 --> 00:30:54.830
Where is he?

156
00:30:56.430 --> 00:30:57.870
Where is he?

157
00:31:02.230 --> 00:31:06.270
- Look how you've grown!
- My knees reach your shoulders.

158
00:31:06.390 --> 00:31:10.670
- Tell me how much you missed Daddy.
- This much.

159
00:31:11.470 --> 00:31:14.030
- Do you know how much I missed you?
- No.

160
00:31:14.750 --> 00:31:16.390
This much!

161
00:31:19.950 --> 00:31:21.070
Go with Mommy.

162
00:32:20.110 --> 00:32:22.790
Don't worry. we'll fix this.

163
00:32:24.070 --> 00:32:26.990
You've always fixed everything.
Remember that.

164
00:32:27.830 --> 00:32:31.590
Daddy. wanna come play with my truck?

165
00:32:32.670 --> 00:32:35.470
Yes. you go to the living room.
I'll be right there.

166
00:32:46.190 --> 00:32:48.230
Your grandfather wants you.

167
00:32:50.270 --> 00:32:51.870
He wants to speak to you.

168
00:32:53.910 --> 00:32:55.430
I'll see you tonight.

169
00:32:58.550 --> 00:33:00.790
Yes. will you put your son to bed?

170
00:33:01.910 --> 00:33:03.150
Get my jacket.

171
00:35:14.190 --> 00:35:16.670
Hi. Stefano.
Sit down.

172
00:35:30.990 --> 00:35:32.550
You must be hungry.

173
00:35:33.830 --> 00:35:35.190
Eat something.

174
00:35:52.390 --> 00:35:55.350
How come you didn't tell me
about America?

175
00:35:58.110 --> 00:36:01.790
You had the cops on your ass
and your contact was dead.

176
00:36:03.070 --> 00:36:07.110
So you tried to take the shipment away
from Emma Lynwood?

177
00:36:07.990 --> 00:36:11.510
I went to offer my condolences.
and get to know them.

178
00:36:12.550 --> 00:36:15.150
The boy let the girl boss him around.

179
00:36:16.870 --> 00:36:19.190
You put important stuff in her hands.

180
00:36:19.870 --> 00:36:23.750
In my opinion they're a couple of fools
with no experience.

181
00:36:25.270 --> 00:36:26.830
Edward's daughter...

182
00:36:27.390 --> 00:36:30.590
I saw her baptized
thirty years ago in America.

183
00:36:32.950 --> 00:36:35.870
I know more than you.

184
00:36:40.150 --> 00:36:43.230
I made a mistake
thinking I was doing right. Grandpa.

185
00:38:26.230 --> 00:38:28.630
- Welcome. Don Minu.
- Benedetto.

186
00:38:28.710 --> 00:38:30.070
Good to see you.

187
00:38:33.750 --> 00:38:35.070
Thank you.

188
00:38:56.590 --> 00:38:57.630
She's ready. Dad.

189
00:39:19.790 --> 00:39:20.790
Here.

190
00:39:26.470 --> 00:39:27.750
Come here!

191
00:39:34.670 --> 00:39:35.910
What's wrong?

192
00:39:37.150 --> 00:39:38.430
Come here!

193
00:39:40.150 --> 00:39:41.790
Hold her still.

194
00:41:51.710 --> 00:41:56.390
What happened to the courier
has put all the families on edge.

195
00:41:58.110 --> 00:41:59.870
The shipment is in transit.

196
00:42:00.670 --> 00:42:03.510
And they haven't asked us
for an extra cent.

197
00:42:03.950 --> 00:42:07.350
The shipment will arrive.
everyone can put their mind at ease.

198
00:42:08.910 --> 00:42:10.550
And if it doesn't arrive?

199
00:42:12.830 --> 00:42:14.550
Then my enemies win

200
00:42:15.390 --> 00:42:18.870
and I die with all those
who are still loyal to me.

201
00:42:21.630 --> 00:42:23.030
This will be few.

202
00:42:24.550 --> 00:42:25.830
Very few.

203
00:42:33.670 --> 00:42:37.750
Don Minu... I've been wanting to talk
to you for a long time.

204
00:42:38.710 --> 00:42:40.110
Then talk.

205
00:42:43.190 --> 00:42:44.710
My son...

206
00:42:46.030 --> 00:42:48.390
took care of a rival.

207
00:42:50.710 --> 00:42:53.270
And now the guy's mother
is asking around.

208
00:42:55.070 --> 00:42:58.390
If we don't tell her what happened.
she'll go to the cops.

209
00:43:01.390 --> 00:43:04.590
Does she know her son is dead?

210
00:43:05.510 --> 00:43:06.790
Yes.

211
00:43:07.390 --> 00:43:10.510
- And that your son killed him?
- Yes. she knows.

212
00:43:14.990 --> 00:43:16.670
She wants to bury him.

213
00:43:17.230 --> 00:43:21.310
With all due respect. Don Minu.
we know what we have to do.

214
00:43:21.990 --> 00:43:24.950
That woman has to be buried
together with her son.

215
00:43:25.270 --> 00:43:28.630
If you'll allow it.
I'll do the job personally.

216
00:43:31.230 --> 00:43:34.950
Women and children
are never to be touched.

217
00:43:39.950 --> 00:43:44.470
Tell people
that when they hear about her son.

218
00:43:45.390 --> 00:43:47.110
they ignore her

219
00:43:47.910 --> 00:43:50.030
and turn away.

220
00:44:05.950 --> 00:44:07.990
Do you mind if I use the bathroom?

221
00:44:09.630 --> 00:44:10.830
Please.

222
00:44:44.150 --> 00:44:45.350
Where are you?

223
00:44:47.390 --> 00:44:48.830
Page 39.

224
00:45:13.270 --> 00:45:16.190
Italo. it's Lucia.
I spoke to Stefano.

225
00:45:16.990 --> 00:45:19.070
They are at Bellantone's house.

226
00:45:35.270 --> 00:45:38.550
Thank you. everybody.
We have to go now.

227
00:45:39.830 --> 00:45:43.310
- You're always welcome. Don Minu.
- Grandpa. it's getting late.

228
00:45:43.950 --> 00:45:48.070
I'm sure Don Benedetto's happy
to put you up for the night.

229
00:45:51.470 --> 00:45:55.590
I've got a place for you. out back.
There's everything you need.

230
00:45:57.190 --> 00:45:59.190
Thanks a lot. Benedetto.

231
00:46:00.950 --> 00:46:05.070
But I need to take my grandson
somewhere else.

232
00:46:05.470 --> 00:46:07.070
Say goodbye. Stefano.

233
00:46:11.030 --> 00:46:13.870
I might come back later tonight.
Benedetto.

234
00:46:23.230 --> 00:46:24.470
Give it to me.

235
00:46:28.950 --> 00:46:32.470
- What?
- Give it to me. don't make me ask again.

236
00:47:38.870 --> 00:47:41.270
You know why the last war started?

237
00:47:43.030 --> 00:47:46.230
They attacked you.
And my father fought back.

238
00:47:49.350 --> 00:47:51.150
That's what they say.

239
00:47:54.390 --> 00:47:55.910
But that's not true.

240
00:47:57.190 --> 00:48:01.590
Your father and Gianni Curtiga
attacked first.

241
00:48:03.630 --> 00:48:07.870
They began this war
to gain control of our organization.

242
00:48:08.750 --> 00:48:11.710
My father would never have done that.

243
00:48:14.230 --> 00:48:17.190
Your father and Curtiga's father

244
00:48:17.790 --> 00:48:21.990
went to the house of a guy who
had been a friend until the day before.

245
00:48:23.150 --> 00:48:26.630
They killed his wife
and his 7-year-old daughter.

246
00:48:26.710 --> 00:48:31.310
- These are just rumors.
- I had no choice. Stefano.

247
00:48:33.150 --> 00:48:38.790
- My father was a gentleman.
- It was the only way to end the war.

248
00:48:40.150 --> 00:48:41.670
He was your son.

249
00:48:43.350 --> 00:48:44.910
He was your blood!

250
00:48:51.270 --> 00:48:53.270
It broke my heart.

251
00:48:53.830 --> 00:48:57.230
but I had to do it
for the good of all the families.

252
00:49:01.310 --> 00:49:03.750
At least now you know the truth.

253
00:49:28.030 --> 00:49:30.230
Don't touch my wife or my son.

254
00:49:56.590 --> 00:49:57.990
Nicola?

255
00:49:58.710 --> 00:49:59.910
Keep moving.

256
00:50:08.590 --> 00:50:10.470
Wait! Nicola!

257
00:50:10.990 --> 00:50:14.910
- Let me go!
- Stay here. Don't move.

258
00:50:22.590 --> 00:50:25.910
Stefano. come here!
You left me alone!

259
00:50:26.150 --> 00:50:28.430
You piece of shit!

260
00:50:37.190 --> 00:50:39.750
You left me alone!

261
00:50:41.270 --> 00:50:45.190
- You left me all alone!
- I can't come. Nicola!

262
00:50:45.390 --> 00:50:48.550
- Stefano. come here!
- I can't.

263
00:50:49.310 --> 00:50:50.710
I can't...

264
00:51:03.670 --> 00:51:05.190
Sorry. Nicola.

265
00:51:22.630 --> 00:51:26.030
The last thing I wanted
in my life was a war.

266
00:51:27.630 --> 00:51:30.310
But now you're bringing it to me.

267
00:51:32.470 --> 00:51:36.150
I'll win this war. Stefano.

268
00:51:39.350 --> 00:51:43.030
After your father died.
I went into hiding.

269
00:51:44.270 --> 00:51:48.310
You were the one
I missed more than anyone.

270
00:51:49.430 --> 00:51:51.710
You were the age your son is now.

271
00:51:53.310 --> 00:51:54.750
Stefano...

272
00:51:56.630 --> 00:51:58.870
I don't want to do to you

273
00:51:59.710 --> 00:52:02.150
what I once did to your father.

274
00:52:04.190 --> 00:52:06.150
You have to choose. Stefano.

275
00:52:08.830 --> 00:52:11.270
Choose which side to take.

276
00:52:17.670 --> 00:52:19.910
You won't get another chance.

277
00:52:21.190 --> 00:52:25.030
Try to move beyond hatred. Stefano.

278
00:54:24.590 --> 00:54:25.950
Who is it?

279
00:54:41.110 --> 00:54:42.550
Franco!

280
00:54:43.710 --> 00:54:45.190
This way.

281
00:54:51.670 --> 00:54:53.070
Go. go!

282
00:55:00.870 --> 00:55:02.150
Go!

283
00:55:20.630 --> 00:55:22.030
Stefano!

284
00:55:26.190 --> 00:55:28.630
- They know everything.
- What happened?

285
00:55:31.430 --> 00:55:34.670
He killed Nicola
right before my eyes!

286
00:55:35.270 --> 00:55:38.550
- Where the fuck's he heading?
- We need to go after him.

287
00:55:38.910 --> 00:55:41.190
Lift him up or he'll bleed out!
Let's go!

288
00:55:42.305 --> 00:56:42.194
